keeper's source is published so you can read it, build it, and check for
yourself what it does with your photographs. That is not the same thing as
open source. This licence says in words what you may do, and nothing extra
is implied by the source being visible.


1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   While keeper is in testing, and it is in testing now, you may use it.
   Free, for anything, on as many machines as you like, at home or at work,
   on your own photographs or on a client's. No payment, no account, no key,
   and no licence check.

   Testing ends on the day a release says it has ended. Every version
   published before that day stays free under this licence forever. A copy
   you already have never stops working and never has to be paid for.

   You may read the source, build it yourself, and change your own copy,
   including inside a company.


2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   You may not sell keeper, licence it, rent it, or charge anybody for it or
   for access to it. Charging a client for the work you did with keeper is
   your business and is not this.

   You may not redistribute keeper or anything built from this source,
   modified or not, under this name or another one. Point people at the
   official release instead.

   You may not run keeper as a service that other people use.

   You may not remove or alter the copyright notices, this licence, or
   NOTICE.


3. WHAT IS NOT GRANTED

   Copyright stays with the author. This is not a patent licence and it is
   not a trademark licence. The name keeper, the wordmark, and the mark are
   not yours to put on your own product.


4. LATER VERSIONS

   Versions published after testing ends may be sold, including under a one
   time paid licence. Those terms will ship with those versions. They cannot
   reach backwards into this one, and they cannot reach into a copy you
   already have.


5. OTHER PEOPLE'S WORK INSIDE KEEPER

   A packaged keeper carries libraries written by other people, each under
   its own licence. Those licences are theirs, not this one, and NOTICE
   names every one of them and where its source is. Nothing in this licence
   takes away anything those licences give you, including the right to
   replace a library with your own build of it.


6. NO WARRANTY

   keeper is provided as is, with no warranty of any kind, express or
   implied, including without limitation the warranties of merchantability,
   fitness for a particular purpose, and noninfringement. To the fullest
   extent the law allows, the author is not liable for any claim, damage, or
   other loss arising from keeper or from its use, including loss of or
   damage to files. keeper reads your photographs and does not write to
   them, and you should still have a backup.


7. IF YOU BREAK THIS LICENCE

   Your permission to use keeper ends. It comes back if you put it right
   within thirty days of being told about it, and you get one of those.


8. CONTRIBUTIONS

   A patch or a pull request you send in, you licence to the author to use,
   change, and distribute, under this licence and under whatever terms
   keeper carries later. You keep your own copyright in it.
